### Frontend vs Backend Balance
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Animation-Performance
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Battle-Flow#Active-Battle-Phase
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#State-Management

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Animation-Standards
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Animation#Performance

Frontend handles (Real-time):
- Target selection (proximity-based ONLY)
- Movement path calculations
- Range validation
- Visual feedback and animations
- Attack timing based on speed stats
- Immediate user interactions
- Current frame state

Backend/Database handles (1s updates):
- Combat calculations
- Health tracking
- Damage resolution
- Node control state
- Victory condition tracking
- Bot loss tracking
- State persistence

### When to Persist
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Damage-Calculation
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Combat-State-Updates
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Flow

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Capture-System#State-Updates
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Sequence#Combat-Flow

1. Critical State Changes (Backend Only):
   - Combat calculations
   - Health updates
   - Node capture events
   - Position validation (every 1 second)
   - Battle phase transitions
   - Victory point calculations
   - Bot losses (type, mark, quantity)

2. Timing of Persistence:
   - Global 1-second timer for all backend updates
   - Phase transitions (pre-battle -> active -> results)
   - Significant events (captures, defeats)
   - Before battle termination

