## Database Schema Guidelines
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#State-Management#State-Categories
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#State-Management#Resource-Management

### Battle State
```typescript
interface BattleState {
  battleId: string;
  phase: 'pre-battle' | 'active' | 'results';
  timeRemaining: number;
  lastUpdated: Date;
  battalions: BattalionState[];
  nodes: NodeState[];
  losses: {
    user: BotLosses[];
    enemy: BotLosses[];
  };
  victoryPoints: {
    user: number;
    enemy: number;
  };
}

interface BotLosses {
  type: 'breacher' | 'guardian' | 'phreak';
  mark: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4;
  quantity: number;
}
```

### Update Frequency
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Combat-Performance#Calculation-Optimization
// - @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#State-Management#Update-Process

High-frequency updates (in-memory):
- Animation states
- Movement calculations
- Visual feedback

Synchronized updates (every 1 second):
- Battalion positions
- Health changes
- Node control changes
- Combat calculations

Low-frequency updates (database):
- Battle phase changes
- Victory calculations
- Final results
- Loss tracking

